{"id":"rel.wave2.batch17.01.preadditive-category.to.small-category","from_formulation":"form.wave2.foundation15.preadditive-category","target_meaning":"meaning.wave2.foundation.small-category","relation_type":"definition_uses","review_state":"screened","source_phrase":"category","editorial_reason":"Hom-set enrichment and bilinear composition are additional structures on an ordinary category, so the Stacks small-category axioms supply the objects, arrows, identities and composition being enriched.","source_locator":"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00ZY","target_locator":"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0013","reviewed_by":"assistant_independent_homological_category_mathematical_review_2026_10_19","human_verified":false}
{"id":"rel.wave2.batch17.02.preadditive-category.to.abelian-group","from_formulation":"form.wave2.foundation15.preadditive-category","target_meaning":"meaning.wave2.foundation.abelian-group","relation_type":"definition_uses","review_state":"screened","source_phrase":"abelian group","editorial_reason":"Each hom-set in a preadditive category is specifically an abelian group, which independently requires a group law and commutativity; this prerequisite does not itself supply composition bilinearity.","source_locator":"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00ZY","target_locator":"https://proofwiki.org/wiki/Definition%3AAbelian_Group","reviewed_by":"assistant_independent_homological_category_mathematical_review_2026_10_19","human_verified":false}
{"id":"rel.wave2.batch17.03.additive-category.to.preadditive-category","from_formulation":"form.wave2.foundation15.additive-category","target_meaning":"meaning.wave2.foundation15.preadditive-category","relation_type":"definition_uses","review_state":"screened","source_phrase":"preadditive category","editorial_reason":"An additive category is a preadditive category with further finite-product data. The underlying abelian-group hom-sets and bilinear composition are prerequisite, not consequences of merely having products.","source_locator":"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0104","target_locator":"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00ZY","reviewed_by":"assistant_independent_homological_category_mathematical_review_2026_10_19","human_verified":false}
{"id":"rel.wave2.batch17.04.abelian-category.to.additive-category","from_formulation":"form.wave2.foundation15.abelian-category","target_meaning":"meaning.wave2.foundation15.additive-category","relation_type":"definition_uses","review_state":"screened","source_phrase":"additive category","editorial_reason":"Stacks 12.5.1 explicitly requires an additive category, then adds all (co)kernels and the coimage-to-image comparison isomorphism. The lower categorical structure is logically prior.","source_locator":"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0109","target_locator":"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0104","reviewed_by":"assistant_independent_homological_category_mathematical_review_2026_10_19","human_verified":false}
{"id":"rel.wave2.batch17.05.abelian-category.to.preadditive-category-kernel","from_formulation":"form.wave2.foundation15.abelian-category","target_meaning":"meaning.wave2.foundation13.preadditive-category-kernel","relation_type":"definition_uses","review_state":"screened","source_phrase":"kernel","editorial_reason":"An abelian category requires the existence of the universal categorical kernel for every arrow, a condition additional to its additive structure. The Stacks 12.3.9 source supplies precisely the universal property.","source_locator":"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0109","target_locator":"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0106","reviewed_by":"assistant_independent_homological_category_mathematical_review_2026_10_19","human_verified":false}
{"id":"rel.wave2.batch17.06.abelian-category.to.preadditive-category-cokernel","from_formulation":"form.wave2.foundation15.abelian-category","target_meaning":"meaning.wave2.foundation13.preadditive-category-cokernel","relation_type":"definition_uses","review_state":"screened","source_phrase":"cokernel","editorial_reason":"All morphisms in an abelian category must admit universal-property cokernels. This is not automatic for arbitrary preadditive categories and uses the separately sourced Stacks 12.3.9 definition.","source_locator":"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0109","target_locator":"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0106","reviewed_by":"assistant_independent_homological_category_mathematical_review_2026_10_19","human_verified":false}
{"id":"rel.wave2.batch17.07.preadditive-category-kernel.to.preadditive-category","from_formulation":"form.wave2.foundation13.preadditive-category-kernel","target_meaning":"meaning.wave2.foundation15.preadditive-category","relation_type":"definition_uses","review_state":"screened","source_phrase":"preadditive category","editorial_reason":"The kernel universal property is formulated in a preadditive category, relying on zero morphisms defined by its abelian-group hom-sets. Kernel existence is not asserted by the prerequisite.","source_locator":"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0106","target_locator":"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00ZY","reviewed_by":"assistant_independent_homological_category_mathematical_review_2026_10_19","human_verified":false}
{"id":"rel.wave2.batch17.08.preadditive-category-cokernel.to.preadditive-category","from_formulation":"form.wave2.foundation13.preadditive-category-cokernel","target_meaning":"meaning.wave2.foundation15.preadditive-category","relation_type":"definition_uses","review_state":"screened","source_phrase":"preadditive category","editorial_reason":"The cokernel universal property requires zero morphisms and composition in a preadditive category, but does not infer its existence for every morphism.","source_locator":"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0106","target_locator":"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00ZY","reviewed_by":"assistant_independent_homological_category_mathematical_review_2026_10_19","human_verified":false}
{"id":"rel.wave2.batch17.09.exact-sequence-abelian-category.to.additive-category","from_formulation":"form.wave2.foundation13.exact-sequence-abelian-category","target_meaning":"meaning.wave2.foundation15.additive-category","relation_type":"definition_uses","review_state":"screened","source_phrase":"additive category","editorial_reason":"The Stacks 12.5.7 definition first considers complexes in additive categories; zero composites and composable arrows are available there even before abelian exactness can be imposed.","source_locator":"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00ZX","target_locator":"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0104","reviewed_by":"assistant_independent_homological_category_mathematical_review_2026_10_19","human_verified":false}
{"id":"rel.wave2.batch17.10.exact-sequence-abelian-category.to.abelian-category","from_formulation":"form.wave2.foundation13.exact-sequence-abelian-category","target_meaning":"meaning.wave2.foundation15.abelian-category","relation_type":"definition_uses","review_state":"screened","source_phrase":"category is abelian","editorial_reason":"Exactness by image equal to kernel requires the abelian hypothesis explicitly stated in Stacks 12.5.7. This link must not imply that merely preadditive or additive categories support the same exactness notion.","source_locator":"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00ZX","target_locator":"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0109","reviewed_by":"assistant_independent_homological_category_mathematical_review_2026_10_19","human_verified":false}
{"id":"rel.wave2.batch17.11.exact-sequence-abelian-category.to.preadditive-category-kernel","from_formulation":"form.wave2.foundation13.exact-sequence-abelian-category","target_meaning":"meaning.wave2.foundation13.preadditive-category-kernel","relation_type":"definition_uses","review_state":"screened","source_phrase":"ker(Y→Z)","editorial_reason":"The exactness condition compares an image to the kernel of the next arrow; this kernel has the universal morphism definition in an abelian category and exists there by its axioms.","source_locator":"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00ZX","target_locator":"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0106","reviewed_by":"assistant_independent_homological_category_mathematical_review_2026_10_19","human_verified":false}
{"id":"rel.wave2.batch17.12.abelian-group-homomorphism-kernel.to.abelian-group","from_formulation":"form.wave2.foundation13.abelian-group-homomorphism-kernel","target_meaning":"meaning.wave2.foundation.abelian-group","relation_type":"definition_uses","review_state":"screened","source_phrase":"abelian groups","editorial_reason":"The concrete homomorphism kernel is the inverse image of the zero element in an abelian group, whose additive identity and subgroup law are prerequisite to the subgroup construction.","source_locator":"https://proofwiki.org/wiki/Definition%3AKernel_of_Group_Homomorphism","target_locator":"https://proofwiki.org/wiki/Definition%3AAbelian_Group","reviewed_by":"assistant_independent_homological_category_mathematical_review_2026_10_19","human_verified":false}
{"id":"rel.wave2.batch17.13.snake-lemma-connecting-map.to.exact-sequence-abelian-category","from_formulation":"form.3d054062d7995be3.snake-lemma-connecting-map","target_meaning":"meaning.wave2.foundation13.exact-sequence-abelian-category","relation_type":"definition_uses","review_state":"screened","source_phrase":"exact rows","editorial_reason":"The snake-lemma diagram assumes exact rows of abelian groups, and Ab is an abelian category. The categorical exact-sequence definition provides the abstract image-equals-kernel prerequisite with this specialization.","source_locator":"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07JV","target_locator":"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00ZX","reviewed_by":"assistant_independent_homological_category_mathematical_review_2026_10_19","human_verified":false}
{"id":"rel.wave2.batch17.14.snake-lemma-connecting-map.to.abelian-group-homomorphism-kernel","from_formulation":"form.3d054062d7995be3.snake-lemma-connecting-map","target_meaning":"meaning.wave2.foundation13.abelian-group-homomorphism-kernel","relation_type":"definition_uses","review_state":"screened","source_phrase":"ker(γ)","editorial_reason":"The connecting homomorphism has as its domain the concrete kernel of the vertical homomorphism γ between abelian groups. This is the additive subgroup definition, not a literal equality with the universal kernel arrow.","source_locator":"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07JV","target_locator":"https://proofwiki.org/wiki/Definition%3AKernel_of_Group_Homomorphism","reviewed_by":"assistant_independent_homological_category_mathematical_review_2026_10_19","human_verified":false}
{"id":"rel.wave2.batch17.15.snake-lemma-connecting-map.to.preadditive-category-cokernel","from_formulation":"form.3d054062d7995be3.snake-lemma-connecting-map","target_meaning":"meaning.wave2.foundation13.preadditive-category-cokernel","relation_type":"definition_uses","review_state":"screened","source_phrase":"coker(α)","editorial_reason":"Its codomain is a cokernel of α in Ab, which can be represented by a quotient group and its projection morphism. The universal cokernel notion underlies that construction, without identifying the arrow with a bare quotient set.","source_locator":"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07JV","target_locator":"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0106","reviewed_by":"assistant_independent_homological_category_mathematical_review_2026_10_19","human_verified":false}
